2026-09-06  David Walther  <david@clearbrookdistillery.com>

	* pdp7fs.h, pdp7fs.c, byteorder.c, byteorder.h, filsys.h, filsys.c,
	mount.filsys.c, fsck.filsys.c, mkfs.filsys.c: wire the word container
	codec into the tools.  filsys_word_codec_by_name() resolves "rb09",
	"packed18" and "rim" (RIM = mkfs7's word2three, three 6-bit frames); a
	new `packing` argument to filsys_open overrides the descriptor's codec,
	mount.filsys takes `-o packing=NAME`, and fsck/mkfs take `-P NAME`.  So a
	PDP-7 dump in any of the three container layouts is a flag, not a rewrite.

2026-09-06  David Walther  <david@clearbrookdistillery.com>

	* pdp7fs.h, pdp7fs.c, v7fs.h, filsys_format.c, byteorder.c, byteorder.h,
	mkfs.filsys.c, fsck.filsys.c: make PDP-7's word container codec a
	descriptor entry.  The SimH RB09 packing (one 18-bit word per 4-byte LE
	slot) was baked into P7_WORDBYTES/P7_BLOCKBYTES/P7_SURFACE1; it is now a
	word_codec_t (get/put/block_bytes) on the descriptor, so a dump from real
	hardware -- which has no reason to use simh's padding -- is a table row
	rather than a rewrite.  word_rb09 (256 bytes/block) is the default;
	word_packed18 (bo_get18packed/bo_put18packed, 18 bits with no gap, 144
	bytes/block) is the packed codec, and lcm(18,8) = 72 bits = 9 bytes per 4
	words makes a 64-word block fill exactly with no ragged tail.

2026-09-06  David Walther  <david@clearbrookdistillery.com>

	* blocktree.c (new), v7fs.h, filsys_format.c, filsys_ops.h, check.c,
	v7fs.c, v1fs.c, pdp7fs.c, filsys.c: fold the block-map tree walk and the
	check helpers into one shared implementation.  The per-backend
	mark_block/mark_tree/mark_blocks, tloop/tloop_from, itrunc/itrunc_from,
	preen, ncheck/ncheck_dir, clri and resolve_dups bodies (the same fifteen
	names four times) collapse into blocktree.c and check.c, driven by two
	descriptor additions: the slot topology (ilarg_mask + large_single/
	large_double, so V6/V1/PDP-7's ILARG reinterpretation is data, not code)
	and the indirect-entry codec (ind_get/ind_put, defaulting to daddr_wid;
	PDP-7 overrides with its 18-bit word).  The vtable loses .itrunc,
	.itrunc_from, .mark_blocks and .preen; .nindir becomes a field (PDP-7's
	container block is 256 bytes of words against a 128-byte logical block,
	so it is not bsize/daddr_wid).  PDP-7 gains an alloc_ops row (pdp7_alloc_ops)
	so the shared walk's bfree/balloc reaches it.
	* The shared walk fixes a latent V6 fsck bug: v6_mark_tree walked slot 7
	(the double-indirect slot) single-level, so a large V6 file's second-level
	blocks were reported missing.
	* test_matrix.c: a V6 large-file regression (write 2000 blocks, past the
	1792-block single-indirect boundary, then fsck) that fails on the old
	single-level walk.

